cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "LEGEND — Mechanistic Intelligence for Rare Disease (WWOX public edition)"
message: "If you use this framework, its disease model, or its learned-gates registry, please cite it."
type: software
abstract: >-
  LEGEND is a public-evidence framework that turns fragmented cross-disciplinary
  literature into an auditable, provenance-tracked disease-mechanism model, while
  recording where AI-assisted reasoning fails and converting each documented failure
  into a reusable, often executable guardrail. The public edition ships the
  disease-agnostic engine (instruction core, epistemic discipline, protocols,
  structural LINT, batch-commit machinery, learned-gates registry, 20 operational
  skills and 5 reusable subagents) together with a de-identified, disease-level model
  of WWOX-related disorders (WOREE / WWOX-DEE and SCAR12) built from public
  literature and public databases only. It contains no individual-level record and is
  not medical advice. Developed in partnership with, and sponsored by, the WWOX
  Foundation, which is the project's sponsor rather than a copyright holder.
authors:
  - name: "The LEGEND project"
contact:
  - name: "WWOX Foundation"
    website: "https://www.wwox.org/"
keywords:
  - rare disease
  - WWOX
  - WOREE
  - developmental and epileptic encephalopathy
  - disease mechanism
  - knowledge graph
  - evidence provenance
  - epistemic discipline
  - failure-aware evaluation
  - AI for science
